-- chem/vertexhop.hypercubical — the hop out of a four-valent vertex along each of its four links. chem/bholonomy.hypercubical's
-- `hop-amp` is the hop along the link coupled first: the vertex holds the electron as ((l0 l1) k, ½) kt with kt
-- coupled to the other two links (l2 l3), and the hop is along l0. Along l1 it is the same with l0 and l1 exchanged.
-- Along l2 or l3 the electron's ½ is first moved from the pair (l0 l1) to the pair (l2 l3): the state
-- ((k ½) kt, kt) 0 is (k, (½ kt) k) 0 times (−1)^(k+½+kt) √((2kt+1)(2k+1)) {k ½ kt; kt 0 k}, and that 6j symbol is
-- (−1)^(k+½+kt) / √((2kt+1)(2k+1)) (`vh-zero`, against Racah's sum of chem/recoupling.hypercubical for k ≤ 1 and
-- kt = k ± ½), so the coefficient is +1: the same state read from the other pair, with k and kt exchanged. The hop
-- along l2 is then `hop-amp` at ((l2 l3) kt, ½) k. `vh-sq` gives the hop's amplitude along link p up to the sign of
-- the links' order; `vh-norm` checks on the smallest vertex (four links of spin ½) that along each of the four
-- links, from each state that exists, the squared amplitudes sum to one. A leaf: no module imports it.
import "bholonomy.hypercubical"

